tan θ = (12)/(5)

**Formula Used:**

tan θ = frac{{opposite}}{{adjacent}}

sin θ = frac{{opposite}}{{hypotenuse}}

{hypotenuse} = sqrt{{opposite}² + {adjacent}²}

**Calculation:**

⇒ Opposite = 12, Adjacent = 5

⇒ {Hypotenuse} = sqrt{12² + 5²}

⇒ {Hypotenuse} = sqrt{144 + 25}

⇒ {Hypotenuse} = sqrt{169}

⇒ {Hypotenuse} = 13

⇒ sin θ = (12)/(13)

**∴ The correct answer is (12)/(13).**

